# Routing for the landing + root-mounted app, served by Cloudflare Workers static
# assets with NO Worker script (wrangler.jsonc has no `main`). Requests matched
# here or by a static asset are free and never count against the Workers quota.
#
#   /                    -> landing home (dist/landing.html, rewrite below)
#   path with a file     -> that file (landing pages, app chunks, robots.txt, ...)
#   any other path       -> app SPA shell (dist/index.html), 200, URL kept:
#                           assets.not_found_handling = "single-page-application"
#
# Rules are first-match and evaluated BEFORE assets, so never add a splat that
# could shadow a landing file. `/` rewrites to `/landing`, not `/landing.html`
# (the latter answers 307 under html_handling).
#
# Firebase Auth's /__/* never reaches this deployment: a zone route sends it to
# the shared sneat-firebase-auth-proxy Worker (sneat-sites repo). Keep `/__`
# paths out of this file. Host-level redirects (www -> apex) are zone Redirect
# Rules, not this file.

# --- Landing home -------------------------------------------------------------
# The root index.html is the app shell (the SPA fallback); the landing owns /.
/               /landing                              200
/landing        /                                     301

# --- Legacy redirects ---------------------------------------------------------
# English is the default locale and owns the bare root.
/en             /                                     301
/en/            /                                     301
# Legacy /pwa/* -> root-mounted route.
/pwa            /                                     301
/pwa/*          /:splat                               301
# Unprefixed legal pages -> the default locale's copy.
/privacy        /en/privacy/ 301
/privacy/       /en/privacy/ 301
/terms          /en/terms/ 301
/terms/         /en/terms/ 301
/vision         /en/vision/ 301
/vision/        /en/vision/ 301
